\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Scatter plot of the JTC dissimilarity versus the Euclidean distance for $100$ random pairs of MNIST digits. The coefficient of determination is \(R^{2}=0.428\). While the $R^2$ value is relatively low, multiple outliers contribute to this reduction. However, the general trend of the data is well captured by the fitted line, indicating a meaningful correlation between JTC dissimilarity and Euclidean distance.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:euclidean_vs_jtc}{{3}{5}{Scatter plot of the JTC dissimilarity versus the Euclidean distance for $100$ random pairs of MNIST digits. The coefficient of determination is \(R^{2}=0.428\). While the $R^2$ value is relatively low, multiple outliers contribute to this reduction. However, the general trend of the data is well captured by the fitted line, indicating a meaningful correlation between JTC dissimilarity and Euclidean distance.\relax }{figure.caption.13}{}}
